# upower -- the power daemon.
#
# gnome-shell's battery indicator, the "low battery" notification, the lid-close
# and idle policies in gnome-settings-daemon, and gnome-control-center's power
# panel are all clients of org.freedesktop.UPower. Without it the shell shows no
# battery at all on a laptop, which is not an error anywhere -- the object it
# watches simply never appears on the bus.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env. The
# GitLab archive URL ends in the tag, so the tarball and its top directory both
# carry the leading "v".
SRC_URL=https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/upower/upower/-/archive/v1.90.9/upower-v1.90.9.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=ca6018535817c2ea687e389e6b47583342154123c0eea0497b409c49dff319b6
SRC_DIR=upower-v1.90.9

# ==============================================================================
# THREE OPTIONS WHOSE DEFAULTS DO NOT BUILD HERE, AND TWO THAT WOULD HAVE
# ==============================================================================
# -Dman, -Dgtk-doc and -Dsystemdsystemunitdir are hard failures at configure
# with their defaults. -Dudevrulesdir and -Dudevhwdbdir are NOT -- they are
# named defensively, and the comment below says why rather than claiming a
# failure that does not happen. Every claim here was checked against the
# tarball or the published package; the udev pair is in this file precisely
# because an earlier draft asserted a failure that a build then disproved.
#
# The shape this tree keeps meeting is in the first three: upstream asks for
# something `required: false` or 'auto' and then insists on it a line later.
#
# -Dman=false and -Dgtk-doc=false. BOTH DEFAULT TO TRUE, and meson.build has
#
#     xsltproc = find_program('xsltproc', disabler: true,
#                             required: get_option('gtk-doc') or get_option('man'))
#
# libxslt IS packaged, so xsltproc is found and the requirement is satisfied --
# and then the build fails inside the XSLT, because the DocBook stylesheets it
# dereferences are not packaged and --nonet forbids fetching them. The failure
# is several minutes in and names a stylesheet URL rather than a build option.
#
# -Dsystemdsystemunitdir=no. The option has no default, so it resolves to '',
# and meson.build then does `systemd_dep = dependency('systemd')` -- REQUIRED,
# not optional -- purely to learn where to install a unit file this system will
# never start. elogind provides libelogind.pc and libsystemd.pc, but NOT
# systemd.pc, so this stops the build outright. 'no' is upstream's own spelling
# for "do not install it".
#
# -Dudevrulesdir and -Dudevhwdbdir. Both default to 'auto', which resolves them
# from `dependency('udev', required: true)` and then
# `udev_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'udev_dir')`.
#
# THESE TWO ARE DEFENSIVE, NOT REQUIRED, and an earlier draft of this comment
# said the opposite -- that eudev ships no udev.pc so the auto path fails at
# configure. It does ship one. Read out of the published package rather than
# assumed:
#
#     $ tar xzOf eudev-3.2.14-2.aarch64.tape.tar.gz \
#           install/usr/share/pkgconfig/udev.pc
#     Name: udev
#     Version: 251
#     udev_dir=/usr/lib/udev
#
# So `dependency('udev')` resolves, udev_dir is /usr/lib/udev, and the auto
# path computes exactly the two paths named below. The build succeeds either
# way and the installed files are identical.
#
# They stay named for the reason the rest of this file names things: the auto
# path depends on eudev continuing to ship a udev.pc SEPARATE from its
# libudev.pc, which is an eudev packaging choice rather than something upower
# requires. If that .pc ever goes, `required: true` makes it a hard configure
# failure, and these two lines are what make that impossible. /usr/lib/udev is
# where eudev actually keeps its rules (its recipe passes --libexecdir=/usr/lib),
# and install.sh asserts the rules landed there rather than trusting the flags.
#
# ==============================================================================
# THE REST
# ==============================================================================
# -Dos_backend=linux. 'auto' would resolve to linux from host_machine.system(),
# so this is the same answer stated rather than derived. It is what makes
# libgudev a hard dependency and what installs the udev rules at all; the
# alternative that would still build is 'dummy', which reports no batteries and
# no line power on every machine.
#
# -Dpolkit=enabled. 'auto' with a disable_auto_if for non-Linux, so it resolves
# on today. Named because polkit is what stops any user on the system from
# calling upowerd's privileged methods, and because a polkit-less build silently
# installs no action file -- there is no error, just an unauthorized daemon.
#
# -Dintrospection=enabled. 'auto'. UPowerGlib-1.0 is what gnome-shell and
# gnome-settings-daemon actually consume.
#
# -Didevice=disabled. 'auto'; libimobiledevice is not packaged, so this is off
# today by accident. It only adds battery reporting for attached iOS devices.
#
# -Dzshcompletiondir=no. The default is '', which installs a zsh completion into
# /usr/share/zsh/site-functions. No zsh is packaged, so that is a file nothing
# can read; 'no' is upstream's spelling for skipping it.
#
# SHIPPED AND LEFT ALONE: the installed-tests. upower has no `tests` option --
# absence from meson_options.txt is not evidence a thing is optional -- so
# src/linux/integration-test.py and upower-integration.test land in
# /usr/libexec/upower and /usr/share/installed-tests/upower unconditionally.
# About 60 KB, and they are dead weight here: nothing runs them, and they need
# python-dbusmock, which is not packaged.
#
# NOT a path-collision risk, which is the question worth asking since several
# GNOME packages ship into /usr/share/installed-tests. Checked in tape rather
# than assumed: daemon/utils/install.go skips directories when building the
# list it conflict-checks ("Directories are created but never recorded in the
# manifest: two packages both shipping /usr/bin must not collide on it"), so
# only FILES can collide, and upower's sit under its own installed-tests/upower
# subdirectory. Removing them would need a second patch to buy back 60 KB and
# is not worth the maintenance.
#
# NOT PASSED: -Dhistorydir and -Dstatedir, which default to
# prefix/localstatedir/lib/upower. meson maps localstatedir to the absolute /var
# when the prefix is /usr (the same mapping measured for fuse3's sysconfdir), so
# the history lands in /var/lib/upower and not in /usr/var.
MESON_ARGS="-Dos_backend=linux -Dpolkit=enabled -Dintrospection=enabled \
-Didevice=disabled -Dman=false -Dgtk-doc=false \
-Dsystemdsystemunitdir=no -Dzshcompletiondir=no \
-Dudevrulesdir=/usr/lib/udev/rules.d -Dudevhwdbdir=/usr/lib/udev/hwdb.d"
